<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">charset</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">set charset</ansi> command toggles between UTF-8 and ASCII
display modes.

<ansi fg="yellow">UTF-8 (default):</ansi>
  Tables, borders, and decorations use Unicode box-drawing
  characters for a polished look. Most modern MUD clients
  (Mudlet, Blightmud, web client) handle these correctly.

<ansi fg="yellow">ASCII:</ansi>
  All box-drawing and decorative characters are converted to
  plain ASCII equivalents (+, -, |, =, #, etc). Use this if
  your client shows garbled characters in tables, status bars,
  or the message of the day.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">set charset</ansi>    Toggle between UTF-8 and ASCII
  <ansi fg="command">set</ansi>            View your current charset setting

Your preference is saved and persists across sessions.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help set</ansi>
